---
import { DEMO_RECORDED_ON } from "../../../data/demo-evidence.ts";
import { CLI, demoGate, NEAR_RPC_DEFAULT } from "../../../data/docs.ts";
import { site } from "../../../data/site.ts";
import type { CodeLine, CodeTab } from "../../ui/code-types.ts";
import CodeBlock from "../../ui/CodeBlock.astro";

/**
 * Quickstart. Prerequisites and build steps are those of README.md "Local quickstart" (Linux or
 * Ubuntu WSL2). The audit flags are from `crates/cli/src/main.rs:95-122`; its defaults point at the
 * final gate, so the demo gate needs both --deployment and --manifest.
 */
const directory = site.repoUrl === null ? "constitution" : (site.repoUrl.split("/").pop() ?? "constitution");
const clone: CodeLine[] =
  site.repoUrl === null
    ? [
        {
          note: "Clone the project repository with its submodules: git clone --recurse-submodules <repository URL>",
        },
      ]
    : [{ cmd: `git clone --recurse-submodules ${site.repoUrl}.git` }];

const prerequisites: CodeTab[] = [
  {
    id: "ubuntu",
    label: "Ubuntu",
    lines: [
      { note: "System packages. Needs an administrator account." },
      { cmd: "sudo apt-get update" },
      {
        cmd: "sudo apt-get install -y build-essential pkg-config libssl-dev ca-certificates git curl make python3",
      },
      { note: "Toolchains, as the user who will build." },
      {
        cmd: "curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh -s -- -y --default-toolchain none",
      },
      { cmd: 'export PATH="$HOME/.cargo/bin:$HOME/.foundry/bin:$PATH"' },
      { cmd: "curl -L https://foundry.paradigm.xyz | bash" },
      { cmd: "foundryup --install 1.8.6" },
    ],
  },
];

const build: CodeTab[] = [
  {
    id: "build",
    label: "Build",
    lines: [
      ...clone,
      { cmd: `cd ${directory}` },
      { cmd: 'export PATH="$HOME/.cargo/bin:$HOME/.foundry/bin:$PATH"' },
      { cmd: "cargo build -p constitution-cli --locked -j 1" },
      { cmd: "forge build --root contracts" },
      { note: "Prints the subcommands." },
      { cmd: `${CLI} --help` },
    ],
  },
];

const audit: CodeTab[] = [
  {
    id: "audit",
    label: "Audit",
    lines: [
      { note: `Reads ${demoGate.account} and compares it with the committed deployment record and rules.` },
      {
        cmd: `${CLI} audit --deployment deployments/demo.json --manifest rules/demo/manifest.json --near-rpc ${site.nearRpc}`,
      },
    ],
  },
];
---

<div class="docs-prose">
  <p>
    You need Linux or Ubuntu on WSL2, not a native Windows shell. These steps build the CLI and
    read public state. They do not need Docker, a wallet, an AI key or a signing key, and they
    send no transaction.
  </p>

  <h3>Before you build</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Git, GNU Make and Rustup. The repository pins its Rust toolchain and installs it on the first Cargo run.</li>
    <li>Foundry <strong>1.8.6</strong>, which provides <code>forge</code> and <code>anvil</code>.</li>
    <li>A C toolchain, <code>pkg-config</code> and the OpenSSL development headers.</li>
  </ul>
  <details class="docs-details">
    <summary>Install them on Ubuntu or WSL2</summary>
    <CodeBlock id="docs-prereq" label="Prerequisites" tabs={prerequisites} title="shell" />
  </details>

  <h3>Build the CLI</h3>
  <p>
    The first build downloads the submodules and compiles every dependency, so it needs a network
    connection, disk space and time. <code>-j 1</code> keeps memory use low.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock id="docs-build" label="Build" tabs={build} title={`${directory}/`} />
  <p class="muted">
    If <code>CARGO_TARGET_DIR</code> is set, use its <code>debug/constitution</code> binary in place
    of <code>./target/debug/constitution</code>.
  </p>

  <h3>Audit the demo gate</h3>
  <p>
    <code>audit</code> reads the gate and the Base Sepolia proxy, then checks them against the
    deployment record and the committed rule set. It changes nothing, and it exits 1 if any check
    fails.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock id="docs-audit" label="Audit" tabs={audit} title={`${directory}/`} />
  <p class="muted">
    The CLI's built-in NEAR endpoint, <code>{NEAR_RPC_DEFAULT}</code>, may rate-limit (HTTP 429)
    under load. So every example on this page passes <code>--near-rpc {site.nearRpc}</code>
    explicitly, the endpoint this page itself reads through.
  </p>
  <p class="docs-note">
    <strong>Read every line, not only the exit code.</strong> The README recorded this audit on
    {DEMO_RECORDED_ON}: it failed only <code>gate_has_no_access_keys</code>, because the demo gate's
    access key was still present. That key was scheduled for deletion on 2026-11-12. State changes,
    so read every line of your own run instead of relying on this record.
  </p>

  <h3>Where to next</h3>
  <p>
    To write an upgrade the rules accept, read the next section. To run a ready-made attack without
    installing anything, open the <a href="/app">live demo</a>.
  </p>
</div>
